# Project structure

| Path | Owner |
| --- | --- |
{% if layout == 'monorepo' %}
{% for component in packages -%}
| `{{ component.path }}/` | {{ component.profile }}: native manifest, source, tests, local environment and lock |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
| `src/` | {{ profile }} product source; the root owns its native manifest, tests, environment and lock |
{% endif %}
| `scripts/`, `bin/` | Repository maintenance and thin command entrypoints, not product policy |
| `tests/` | Native tests for a single package; actual cross-package tests for a monorepo |
| `docs/specs/`, `docs/adr/` | Maintained project contracts and decision rationale |
| `.agents/` | Project routing/setup; no reusable skill bodies or generic blank forms |
| `.codex/config.toml`, `.claude/settings.json` | Team plugin activation; not installation or trust proof |

{% if layout == 'monorepo' %}
`apps/` contains deployable applications/services; `packages/` contains reusable code when selected. Each package keeps
its language-native inner `src/`. No empty outer `src/` or unused group is created. Co-location does not implement
interoperability or one shared toolchain, lock, deployment or workspace; adopt native workspaces for actual dependencies.
{% endif %}
This describes fresh generation, not a code/folder migration on update. Actual manifests and package READMEs prevail.
Use `.gitkeep` only for necessary otherwise-empty locations; an existing README already keeps a folder in Git.
